In <4b8D02hl10rd01@JUTS.ccc.amdahl.com> jdg00@ccc.amdahl.com (Josh Grosse) writes:

>In my MS-DOS 5 CONFIG.SYS I've got two records that appear to be the cause
>of the problem:
>          DOS=HIGH,UMB
>          DEVICEHIGH=C:\.....
>I load a device driver that can run above the 640K line.
>If I drop this driver back below the line by changing these lines to:
>          DOS=HIGH
>          DEVICE=C:\.....
>My problem goes away (once I remove RAWIO, of course).  I've been
>working with Mike Gallop (mikey@binkley.cs.mcgill.ca) on this problem,
>and perhaps with this new insight he can figure out what the root cause
>is.

Funny, I've got lots of stuff loaded high in the UMB area, and I can run NH
inside of Windows (3.1) without any problem in 386 Enhanced mode.

My .pif is as follows:

Name: NETHACK.EXE
startup dir: C:\NETHACK

KB REQUIRED: 0
KB DESIRED: 640


This seems to run quite well both in full screen and windowed mode. 

Also, I just left my .cnf the way it was and did NOT rmove the rawio command.

Joe

